      "body": "## Motivation\n\nQuark MXFP4 W4A4 dense linears (`QuarkW4A4MXFP4`, Triton path) crash under `--enable-torch-compile` on ROCm because the fake impl of `sglang::aiter_dynamic_mxfp4_quant` declares a row-major block scale while aiter returns a column-major one; this PR allocates the fake scale the way aiter does. aiter's `dynamic_mxfp4_quant` returns `torch.empty((N/32, M)).T` with stride `(1, M)`, the fake returns a contiguous `(M, N/32)`, and Inductor emits an `assert_size_stride` from the fake that fails during CUDA-graph capture:\n\n```\nAssertionError: expected size 4==4, stride 1==128 at dim=0; expected size 128==128, stride 4==1 at dim=1\nError in op: torch.ops.sglang.aiter_dynamic_mxfp4_quant.default\n```\n\nReproduced on MI355X at main@f85ca901e2 with `Qwen3-8B --quantization quark_mxfp4 --enable-torch-compile`; the server came up and generated normally with this fix. No default configuration reaches the path: it needs ROCm with `--enable-torch-compile` (off by default), plus checkpoints with Quark MXFP4 dense linears (e.g. layers 0-2 of GLM-5.3-Quark-MXFP4-AttnFP8) or online `--quantization quark_mxfp4`.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Allocate the fake's block scale exactly like aiter: a `(ceil(N/32), M)` buffer, transposed.\n- Add a regression test to `test_quark_mxfp4_asm.py` that runs the op under `FakeTensorMode` and checks the scale's shape and `(1, M)` stride. It needs a ROCm build with aiter but no GPU, so the file is also registered for AMD CI.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: the fake only describes output metadata for tracing; eager numerics are unchanged.\n\nThe new test, run CPU-only at main@b45a36531c:\n\n| tree | result |\n|---|---|\n| main | fails: stride `(65, 1) != (1, 37)` |\n| scale allocated transposed, then `.contiguous()` | fails: stride `(65, 1) != (1, 37)` |\n| `(M, N/32)` buffer transposed | fails: shape `(65, 37) != (37, 65)` |\n| this PR | passes |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nTBD on current main. No performance change is claimed; this unblocks `--enable-torch-compile` for these layers.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n---\n\nFound by [Hyperloom](https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Hyperloom); reviewed and measured by hand.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #41427222190](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41427222190)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41427222089](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41427222089)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41427222028](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41427222028)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
